    "difficultyReason": "Every part is a single linear absolute-value inequality solved by the taught two-case method. The hardest parts, such as |4x-3|>5 and |5x+4|>=6, need only one split into cases, simple rearrangement and a choice between 'and' and 'or'. This is slightly above p16-q1, where the graph does the reading, because the student must now pick the case structure and the direction of the sign flip without a graph. It stays below the routine linked procedures of p5-q2 and p17-q4, which add sketching, fractional forms or other extra steps.",
